# AI_OS — Environment Configuration Example
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust for your environment:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored and must never be committed. This file must never
# contain a real secret value — secrets are referenced, not embedded
# (ADR-0024: docs/18_decision_log/adr/ADR-0024-secrets-management-backend.md).
#
# Full variable reference: docs/03_architecture/services/configuration_management.md
# and docs/11_deployment/deployment_architecture.md.

# --- The bootstrap minimum (read directly from the environment; see
# docs/03_architecture/services/configuration_management.md §3.3) ---
#
# AIOS_ENV/AIOS_ROLE decide WHICH configuration files this process reads
# (config/platform.yaml + infra/environments/<env>.yaml) — they cannot
# themselves live in those files. Everything else (host, port, log
# level, capability pack directories, ...) is configured in
# config/platform.yaml and infra/environments/<env>.yaml, not here.

# Selects the environment configuration layer. One of: local, dev, staging, production.
AIOS_ENV=local

# Which process role this instance runs. One of: api, worker.
AIOS_ROLE=api

# PostgreSQL connection (persistence/settings.py:DatabaseSettings). No
# default — a missing value fails clearly at startup rather than
# silently pointing nowhere.
# AIOS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://aios:password@localhost:5432/aios

# Base OpenTelemetry Collector endpoint for real OTLP/HTTP export
# (observability/settings.py:ObservabilitySettings, ADR-0017,
# P01-S05-M04-T03). Unset (the default in every environment today, no
# Collector deployed) keeps the console exporters. 4318 is the
# Collector's standard OTLP/HTTP receiver port (4317 is OTLP/gRPC, not
# what this Kernel's exporter speaks).
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318

# --- Reserved for later Stage A/B steps — not yet read by any code --------
# Uncomment and configure as each component lands.

# AIOS_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
# AIOS_SECRET_BACKEND=env

# Anthropic API key, resolved via EnvSecretProvider (ADR-0024, local
# development only) at the reference `secret://env/llm/anthropic-api-key`.
# Read by AnthropicAdapter through build_anthropic_adapter — never by
# the Anthropic SDK's own ANTHROPIC_API_KEY auto-detection, and never
# embedded in this file with a real value.
# AIOS_SECRET_LLM_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Pre-shared HS256 signing key for the minimal Security Manager's bearer
# token verifier (ai_os_kernel.security_manager.token_verifier), resolved
# via EnvSecretProvider at `secret://env/security/jwt-signing-key`. Not
# full OIDC — see that module's docstring for the documented upgrade
# path. A missing value denies every request to a protected route
# (fail closed), it does not disable authentication. Use a long, random
# value in any real environment; never embed a real value in this file.
# AIOS_SECRET_SECURITY_JWT_SIGNING_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-value
